### Description

This Terraform program creates an AWS Kendra data source with a proxy configuration. It includes the necessary IAM role and policy to allow the Kendra data source to access required resources. The configuration is designed to be deployable with Terraform version ~> 1.9.8 and the AWS provider version ~> 5.75.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "kendra_data_source_role" {
  name = "kendra-data-source-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "kendra.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "kendra_data_source_policy" {
  name = "kendra-data-source-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.kendra_data_source_role.arn

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "s3:GetObject",
          "s3:ListBucket"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = [
          "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name",
          "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket-name/*"
        ]
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source_with_proxy" {
  index_id = "your-kendra-index-id"
  name     = "kendra-data-source-with-proxy"
  type     = "WEBCRAWLER"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.kendra_data_source_role.arn

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      urls {
        seed_url_configuration {
          seed_urls = [
            "https://example.com"
          ]
        }
      }
      proxy_configuration {
        host = "proxy.example.com"
        port = 8080
        credentials = "arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:123456789012:secret:your-secret-name"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### Notes

- Replace `"your-bucket-name"` with the actual S3 bucket name.
- Replace `"your-kendra-index-id"` with the actual Kendra index ID.
- Replace `"https://example.com"` with the actual seed URL for the web crawler.
- Replace `"proxy.example.com"` and `8080` with the actual proxy host and port.
- Replace `"arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:123456789012:secret:your-secret-name"` with the actual ARN of the AWS Secrets Manager secret containing the proxy credentials.

