### Description
This Terraform program creates an AWS Kendra data source with URL exclusion and inclusion patterns. It includes the necessary configuration for the Kendra data source and ensures that the AWS provider is properly configured with the appropriate region and credentials.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_kendra_index" "example" {
  name        = "example-kendra-index"
  role_arn    = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/kendra-role"  # Replace with your IAM role ARN
  description = "Example Kendra Index"
}

resource "aws_kendra_data_source" "kendra_data_source" {
  index_id      = aws_kendra_index.example.id
  name          = "example-kendra-data-source"
  type          = "WEBCRAWLER"

  configuration {
    web_crawler_configuration {
      url_exclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/exclude/*"]
      url_inclusion_patterns = ["https://example.com/include/*"]
    }
  }

  role_arn = "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/kendra-crawler-role"  # Replace with your IAM role ARN for crawling
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`. You can change this to your preferred region.
2. **Kendra Index**: An AWS Kendra index is created with a specified name, role ARN, and description.
3. **Kendra Data Source**: A Kendra data source is created with the type `WEBCRAWLER`. The `configuration` block includes `web_crawler_configuration` with `url_exclusion_patterns` and `url_inclusion_patterns` to specify which URLs to exclude and include during the crawling process.
4. **IAM Role ARNs**: Replace the placeholder IAM role ARNs with the actual ARNs of your IAM roles.

This configuration ensures that the Kendra data source is properly set up with the specified URL patterns for exclusion and inclusion.

