### Description
This Terraform configuration sets up a DynamoDB table with on-demand capacity mode. The table is configured with a hash key and an optional range key. The on-demand throughput settings are also specified to control the maximum read and write request units.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"  # Specify your desired AWS region
}

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "dynamodb_table" {
  name         = "GameScores"
  billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"  # On-demand capacity mode
  hash_key     = "UserId"
  range_key    = "GameTitle"

  attribute {
    name = "UserId"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "GameTitle"
    type = "S"
  }

  attribute {
    name = "TopScore"
    type = "N"
  }

  on_demand_throughput {
    max_read_request_units  = 1000
    max_write_request_units = 1000
  }

  tags = {
    Name        = "dynamodb-table-1"
    Environment = "production"
  }
}
```

This configuration creates a DynamoDB table named `GameScores` with on-demand capacity mode. The table has a hash key `UserId` and an optional range key `GameTitle`. The `on_demand_throughput` block specifies the maximum read and write request units. The table is tagged for easy identification.

