Below is a complete Terraform HCL program that creates an AWS SageMaker Notebook Instance with the specified requirements. The program includes the necessary IAM role and policy to ensure the notebook instance has the required permissions.

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

# Create an IAM role for the SageMaker notebook instance
resource "aws_iam_role" "sagemaker_notebook_role" {
  name = "sagemaker-notebook-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "sagemaker.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Attach a policy to the IAM role
resource "aws_iam_role_policy" "sagemaker_notebook_policy" {
  name = "sagemaker-notebook-policy"
  role = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_notebook_role.id

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "sagemaker:*",
          "ec2:*",
          "cloudwatch:*",
          "logs:*",
          "s3:*"
        ]
        Effect = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

# Create the SageMaker notebook instance
resource "aws_sagemaker_notebook_instance" "sagemaker_notebook_instance" {
  name          = "my-sagemaker-notebook"
  role_arn      = aws_iam_role.sagemaker_notebook_role.arn
  instance_type = "ml.t2.medium"

  # Optional: Additional code repositories
  additional_code_repositories = [
    "https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws.git"
  ]

  # Optional: Tags
  tags = {
    Name = "MySageMakerNotebook"
  }
}
```

This Terraform configuration does the following:
1. Sets up the AWS provider with the region `us-west-2`.
2. Creates an IAM role named `sagemaker-notebook-role` with a trust policy allowing SageMaker to assume the role.
3. Attaches a policy to the IAM role granting broad permissions for SageMaker, EC2, CloudWatch, Logs, and S3 operations.
4. Creates a SageMaker notebook instance named `my-sagemaker-notebook` with the specified IAM role and instance type `ml.t2.medium`.
5. Adds an additional code repository from the specified GitHub URL.
6. Tags the notebook instance for easy identification.

This configuration ensures that the SageMaker notebook instance has the necessary permissions and is properly set up with the specified code repository.

