### Description
This Terraform configuration creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an HTTP listener that redirects all incoming HTTP traffic to HTTPS. The configuration includes an IAM role and policy for the load balancer, although in this specific setup, the IAM role and policy are not strictly necessary for the redirection functionality. They are included as placeholders for more complex configurations where additional permissions might be required.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0fedcba9876543210"]
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]

  enable_deletion_protection = true

  tags = {
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "listener_http" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.load_balancer.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "redirect"

    redirect {
      port        = "443"
      protocol    = "HTTPS"
      status_code = "HTTP_301"
    }
  }
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "lb_role" {
  name = "my-alb-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticloadbalancing.amazonaws.com"
        }
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "lb_policy" {
  name        = "my-alb-policy"
  description = "Policy for ALB"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Action = [
          "ec2:Describe*",
          "elasticloadbalancing:*"
        ]
        Effect   = "Allow"
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_lb_policy" {
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.lb_policy.arn
  role       = aws_iam_role.lb_role.name
}
```

### Explanation
1. **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured with the region `us-west-2`.
2. **Load Balancer (ALB)**: An Application Load Balancer is created with two subnets and a security group. Deletion protection is enabled to prevent accidental deletion.
3. **HTTP Listener**: An HTTP listener is created on port 80. It has a default action that redirects all traffic to HTTPS on port 443 with a 301 status code.
4. **IAM Role and Policy**: An IAM role and policy are created for the load balancer. The role assumes the Elastic Load Balancing service, and the policy grants broad permissions for demonstration purposes. In a production environment, you should restrict permissions to what is necessary.

