LLM Output #0:
### Description

This Terraform configuration sets up an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with an "authenticate-cognito" action. The ALB will authenticate users using Amazon Cognito. The configuration includes the following resources:

1. **AWS Load Balancer (ALB)**: An Application Load Balancer to distribute incoming traffic.
2. **AWS Cognito User Pool**: A user pool for managing user identities.
3. **AWS Cognito User Pool Client**: A client associated with the user pool.
4. **AWS IAM Role**: An IAM role for the load balancer to authenticate with Cognito.
5. **AWS IAM Policy**: An IAM policy granting necessary permissions to the IAM role.
6. **AWS IAM Role Policy Attachment**: Attaches the IAM policy to the IAM role.
7. **AWS Load Balancer Listener**: A listener on the load balancer to handle incoming HTTP requests.
8. **AWS Load Balancer Listener Rule**: A listener rule to route traffic based on conditions.
9. **AWS Load Balancer Authenticate Cognito Action**: An action to authenticate users using Cognito.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "front_end" {
  name               = "front-end-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"
  security_groups    = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]  # Replace with your security group ID
  subnets            = ["subnet-0123456789abcdef0", "subnet-0123456789abcdef1"]  # Replace with your subnet IDs

  enable_deletion_protection = true

  tags = {
    Environment = "production"
  }
}

resource "aws_cognito_user_pool" "pool" {
  name = "my-user-pool"

  admin_create_user_config {
    allow_admin_create_user_only = false
  }

  password_policy {
    minimum_length                = 8
    require_lowercase             = true
    require_numbers               = true
    require_symbols               = true
    require_uppercase             = true
    temporary_password_validity_days = 7
  }

  schema {
    attribute_data_type = "String"
    name                = "email"
    required            = true
  }

  schema {
    attribute_data_type = "String"
    name                = "phone_number"
    required            = true
  }
}

resource "aws_cognito_user_pool_client" "client" {
  name         = "my-app-client"
  user_pool_id = aws_cognito_user_pool.pool.id

  generate_secret = true
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "lb_auth_role" {
  name = "lb-auth-role"

  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Principal = {
          Service = "elasticloadbalancing.amazonaws.com"
        }
        Action = "sts:AssumeRole"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_policy" "lb_auth_policy" {
  name = "lb-auth-policy"

  policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17"
    Statement = [
      {
        Effect = "Allow"
        Action = [
          "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPoolClient",
          "cognito-idp:ListUserPoolClients",
          "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPoolDomain",
          "cognito-idp:DescribeUserPool"
        ]
        Resource = "*"
      }
    ]
  })
}

resource "aws_iam_role_policy_attachment" "attach_lb_auth_policy" {
  policy_arn = aws_iam_policy.lb_auth_policy.arn
  role       = aws_iam_role.lb_auth_role.name
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "front_end" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.front_end.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type = "authenticate-cognito"

    authenticate_cognito {
      user_pool_arn       = aws_cognito_user_pool.pool.arn
      user_pool_client_id = aws_cognito_user_pool_client.client.id
      user_pool_domain    = "my-user-pool-domain"  # Replace with your Cognito user pool domain
    }
  }

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = "arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-west-2:123456789012:targetgroup/my-target-group/1234567890123456"  # Replace with your target group ARN
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener_rule" "listener_rule" {
  listener_arn = aws_lb_listener.front_end.arn
  priority     = 1

  action {
    type = "forward"

    forward {
      target_group {
        arn = "arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-west-2:123456789012:targetgroup/my-target-group/1234567890123456"  # Replace with your target group ARN
      }
    }
  }

  condition {
    field  = "host-header"
    values = ["example.com"]  # Replace with your domain
  }
}
```

### Notes

1. **Security Groups and Subnets**: Replace the placeholder security group and subnet IDs with your actual AWS resource IDs.
2. **Cognito User Pool Domain**: Replace `"my-user-pool-domain"` with your actual Cognito user pool domain.
3. **Target Group ARN**: Replace the placeholder target group ARN with your actual target group ARN.
4. **Domain**: Replace `"example.com"` with your actual domain.

This configuration ensures that the load balancer is set up to authenticate users using Amazon Cognito, with the necessary IAM roles and policies in place.

