### Description

This Terraform program creates an Application Load Balancer (ALB) with a target group and attaches a listener to the ALB that forwards traffic to the target group. The ALB is configured to handle HTTP traffic on port 80. The target group is set up to balance traffic across EC2 instances running in a specific VPC.

### Terraform HCL Program

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-west-2"
}

resource "aws_lb" "load_balancer" {
  name               = "my-alb"
  internal           = false
  load_balancer_type = "application"

  subnet_mapping {
    subnet_id = "subnet-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your subnet ID
  }

  security_groups = ["sg-0123456789abcdef0"]  # Replace with your security group ID

  enable_deletion_protection = false
}

resource "aws_lb_target_group" "target_group" {
  name     = "my-target-group"
  port     = 80
  protocol = "HTTP"
  vpc_id   = "vpc-0123456789abcdef0"  # Replace with your VPC ID

  health_check {
    path                = "/"
    interval            = 30
    timeout             = 5
    healthy_threshold   = 5
    unhealthy_threshold = 2
  }
}

resource "aws_lb_listener" "listener" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.load_balancer.arn
  port              = "80"
  protocol          = "HTTP"

  default_action {
    type             = "forward"
    target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.target_group.arn
  }
}
```

### Notes

- **Provider Configuration**: The AWS provider is configured to use the `us-west-2` region. You can change this to any other region as needed.
- **Subnet and Security Group**: Replace the placeholder subnet and security group IDs with actual IDs from your AWS account.
- **VPC ID**: Replace the placeholder VPC ID with the ID of the VPC where your target instances are located.
- **Health Check**: The health check is configured to use HTTP on port 80 with a path of `/`. Adjust the path and other parameters as needed for your application.
- **Listener**: The listener is configured to forward traffic to the target group on port 80 using the HTTP protocol. Adjust the port and protocol if your application requires different settings.

